.TH GTDO 1 "2026-08-10" "gtdo dev" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gtdo \- a Go port of the todo.txt-cli (todo.sh) command line interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gtdo
.RI [ options ]
.B action
.RI [ task_number ]
.RI [ task_description ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gtdo
is a Go port of
.BR todo.txt-cli ,
the todo.sh command line interface for maintaining todo lists in
.IR todo.txt
format: one task per line, optionally tagged with a priority
.RI ((A) ),
a creation date, and
.B @context
and
.B +project
tags.
.PP
Output, prompts, and exit codes match todo.sh byte for byte for the twenty
ported todo.sh actions. Configuration follows todo.sh: command line options,
environment variables, and a configuration file.
.PP
Shell completion is built in: the
.B completion
command generates completion scripts for bash, zsh, fish, and powershell,
and the actions complete task numbers and
.B @context
and
.B +project
tags from the current
.IR todo.txt
file.
.PP
As an additional gtdo extension, the
.B format [FILE]
action rewrites both configured task files, or the selected file when
.I FILE
is specified.
.PP
Interactive add modes are available with
.B gtdo add \-i
or
.B gtdo add \-g .
The guided form runs metadata, project, and context phases; repeatable
.B --only
options select one or more phases. Candidate values come only from the
configured
.B todo_file
and
.B done_file
paths; the configured
.B report_file
is not scanned. Terminal selectors support Up/Down, Space, /, Enter, and Esc.
When standard input is not a terminal, the modes use a line-oriented protocol
without prompts or escape sequences.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B add
Add a TODO item to todo.txt.
.TP
.B addm
Add multiple TODO items to todo.txt.
.TP
.B addto
Add a line of text to a file in the todo.txt directory.
.TP
.B append
Append text to the task on line NR.
.TP
.B archive
Move done tasks from todo.txt to done.txt and remove blank lines.
.TP
.B del
Delete the task on line NR, or remove TERM from it.
.TP
.B depri
Remove the priority from the task(s) on line NR.
.TP
.B do
Mark task(s) on line NR as done.
.TP
.B format
Rewrite task files using the configured format.
.TP
.B help
Display help about usage, options and built-in actions, or just the usage help for the passed ACTION(s).
.TP
.B list
Display all tasks in todo.txt.
.TP
.B listall
Display all the lines in todo.txt AND done.txt.
.TP
.B listcon
List all the task contexts that start with the @ sign in todo.txt.
.TP
.B listpri
Display all tasks prioritized PRIORITIES.
.TP
.B listproj
List all the projects (terms that start with a + sign) in todo.txt.
.TP
.B move
Move a task from one file to another in the todo.txt directory.
.TP
.B prepend
Prepend text to the task on line NR.
.TP
.B pri
Add or replace the priority of the task on line NR.
.TP
.B replace
Replace the task on line NR.
.TP
.B report
Add the number of open and done tasks to report.txt.
.TP
.B shorthelp
List the one-line usage of all built-in actions.

.SH CONFIGURATION
.PP
gtdo reads strict camelCase JSON configuration from
.IR ~/.config/gtdo/config.json
unless another path is selected with
.B \-d
or
.B $GTDO_CONFIG .
.PP
Timestamp IDs are opt in. Set
.B behaviour.enableUUID
to true in the JSON configuration, or use
.B GTDO_ENABLE_UUID .
When enabled, each newly created task receives a UTC timestamp ID in the exact format
.B YYYYMMDDTHHMMSS.nnZ
(for example,
.B 20260808T143045.12Z ) .
If a candidate collides with an existing ID, or with one allocated earlier in
the same batch, gtdo advances it by 10 ms and retries. IDs are creation-only
and are preserved through edits and moves; enabling the setting later never
backfills existing tasks.
.PP
The former date-on-add behavior has been retired, so add commands no longer
insert a creation date automatically. Dates already present in a task remain
unchanged.
.SH INTERACTIVE ADD
.PP
The mode options are
.B \-i
or
.B --interactive
for one editable task line, and
.B \-g
or
.B --guided
for phased input. Guided phase selection repeats
.B --only
with the phase names metadata, project, and context.
.TP
.B gtdo add \-i
Read one editable task line. On a terminal, @context and +project words offer
completion from the configured todo and done files. With non-TTY input, read
one plain task line.
.TP
.B gtdo add \-g
Read a task, then run the metadata, project, and context phases in that order.
The project and context phases use searchable multi-selectors. Their controls
are Up/Down to move, Space to toggle, / to filter, Enter to confirm, and Esc
to clear a filter or exit.
.TP
.B gtdo add \-g --only metadata|project|context
Run only the named guided phase(s). Repeat
.B --only
to select more than one phase; it requires guided mode. The task line is
always read.
.PP
Candidates are deduplicated from the configured
.B todo_file
and
.B done_file
paths only. The configured
.B report_file
is never scanned. In the non-TTY protocol, interactive mode consumes one task
line. Guided mode consumes one task line, then input for each enabled phase in
order: zero or more metadata
.B key:value
lines terminated by an empty line, one space-separated project line, and one
space-separated context line. Phases omitted with
.B --only
consume no line. Empty selection lines are valid.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-@
Hide context names in list output.  Use twice to show context names (default).
.TP
.B \-+
Hide project names in list output.  Use twice to show project names (default).
.TP
.B \-c
Color mode
.TP
.BI \-d " CONFIG_FILE"
Use a configuration file other than one of the defaults
.TP
.B \-f
Forces actions without confirmation or interactive input
.TP
.B \-h
Display a short help message; same as action "shorthelp"
.TP
.B \-p
Plain mode turns off colors
.TP
.B \-P
Hide priority labels in list output.  Use twice to show priority labels (default).
.TP
.B \-a
Don't auto-archive tasks automatically on completion
.TP
.B \-A
Auto-archive tasks automatically on completion
.TP
.B \-n
Don't preserve line numbers; automatically remove blank lines on task deletion
.TP
.B \-N
Preserve line numbers
.TP
.B \-v
Verbose mode turns on confirmation messages
.TP
.B \-vv
Extra verbose mode prints some debugging information and additional help text
.TP
.B \-V
Displays version and build information
.TP
.B \-x
No-op; accepted for compatibility with todo.txt-cli
.PP
gtdo reads configuration from JSON files.  The following keys have no
environment-variable or command-line equivalents.  Place these keys in the
.B behaviour
object.
.TP
.B behaviour.enableUUID
When true, add, addm, and addto assign UTC timestamp IDs to new tasks. IDs
advance in 10 ms steps on collisions, are preserved through edits and moves,
and never backfill existing tasks.
.TP
.B allowedContexts
An array of complete context tokens, such as
.BR @work
and
.BR @home .
When this key is omitted, contexts are unrestricted.  An explicit empty array
rejects every context tag.  Matching is exact and case-sensitive.
.TP
.B allowedProjects
An array of complete project tokens, such as
.BR +gtdo
and
.BR +personal .
When this key is omitted, projects are unrestricted.  An explicit empty array
rejects every project tag.  Matching is exact and case-sensitive.
.PP
gtdo validates final task text for
.BR add ,
.BR addm ,
.BR addto ,
.BR append ,
.BR prepend ,
and
.BR replace .
Listing remains usable for legacy tasks with tags that are not allowed.
On rejection, the diagnostic includes the file and 1-based line number, for
example:
.BR "TODO: Context \"@home\" is not allowed in /path/to/todo.txt at line 3."
.TP
.B behaviour.taskFormat
Controls the field order used by the
.B format
action. The default is
.BR [checked][priority][uuid][content][keywords][project][context] .
The formatter inserts one space between non-empty fields automatically. The
available fields are
.BR checked ,
.BR priority ,
.BR uuid ,
.BR content ,
.BR keywords ,
.BR project ,
and
.BR context .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TODO_DIR
Path to the directory that holds the todo files.
.TP
.B TODO_FILE
Path to the todo.txt file.
.TP
.B DONE_FILE
Path to the done.txt file.
.TP
.B REPORT_FILE
Path to the report.txt file.
.TP
.B TODOTXT_AUTO_ARCHIVE
Same as option \-a (0) or \-A (1).
.TP
.B TODOTXT_FORCE=1
Same as option \-f.
.TP
.B TODOTXT_PRESERVE_LINE_NUMBERS
Same as option \-n (0) or \-N (1).
.TP
.B TODOTXT_PLAIN
Same as option \-p (1) or \-c (0).
.TP
.B TODOTXT_PRIORITY_ON_ADD=pri
Default priority A\-Z.
.TP
.B GTDO_ENABLE_UUID
Same as the
.B behaviour.enableUUID
behavior setting. When enabled, new tasks receive UTC timestamp IDs in the
.B YYYYMMDDTHHMMSS.nnZ
format.
.TP
.B TODOTXT_VERBOSE=1
Same as option \-v.
.TP
.B TODOTXT_DEFAULT_ACTION=""
Run this when called with no arguments.
.TP
.B TODOTXT_SOURCEVAR=$DONE_FILE
Use another source for listcon, listproj.
.TP
.B SENTENCE_DELIMITERS=,.:;
Suppress the added space in append.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $TODO_DIR/todo.txt
The active todo list; defaults to
.IR ~/todo.txt .
.TP
.I $TODO_DIR/done.txt
Completed tasks; defaults to
.IR ~/done.txt .
.TP
.I $TODO_DIR/report.txt
The report output; defaults to
.IR ~/report.txt .
.TP
.I ~/.config/gtdo/config.json
User configuration, searched after the
.B \-d
option and
.BR $GTDO_CONFIG ,
before
.IR /etc/gtdo/config.json .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Generic error: usage errors, unknown actions, and action failures.
.SH SEE ALSO
The todo.txt format: https://github.com/todotxt/todo.txt
.PP
The todo.txt-cli project: https://github.com/todotxt/todo.txt-cli
